[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020660695","pull_request_review_id":2728641120,"id":2020660695,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc54cNXX","diff_hunk":"@@ -609,30 +609,24 @@ class Object {\n \n \ttemplate <class T>\n \tstatic T *cast_to(Object *p_object) {\n-#ifndef NO_SAFE_CAST\n-\t\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\n-#else\n+\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_base_of<Object, T>::value, \"T must be derived from Object\");","path":"core/object.h","commit_id":"be6f971f4ff7b3647ac576ddc5813d462fe6fec9","original_commit_id":"429f1a82b012c3ebd40bab335c5a234cd72cf04b","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"If you're not adding the fallback to `dynamic_cast`, I'd definitely like to see it as a `static_assert`:\r\n```suggestion\r\n\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_base_of<Object, T>::value, \"T must be derived from Object\");\r\n\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_same_v<std::decay_t<T>, typename T::self_type>, \"T must use GDCLASS\");\r\n```","created_at":"2025-03-31T09:07:41Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T09:07:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020660695","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020660695"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020660695"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020660695/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":622,"original_line":622,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020674339","pull_request_review_id":2728663149,"id":2020674339,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc54cQsj","diff_hunk":"@@ -609,30 +609,24 @@ class Object {\n \n \ttemplate <class T>\n \tstatic T *cast_to(Object *p_object) {\n-#ifndef NO_SAFE_CAST\n-\t\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\n-#else\n+\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_base_of<Object, T>::value, \"T must be derived from Object\");","path":"core/object.h","commit_id":"be6f971f4ff7b3647ac576ddc5813d462fe6fec9","original_commit_id":"429f1a82b012c3ebd40bab335c5a234cd72cf04b","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ah actually that flags up it turns out it is being used in a couple of places indirectly, in crypto and mbedTLS, so it may need some backup path after all.\r\n\r\nI'm not quite sure yet how these libraries are actually working _at the moment_ on web and Android actually, given that `dynamic_cast` doesn't seem available on those platforms. :thinking: \r\n\r\nMaybe it's currently working in those two cases by effectively doing a cast check _only_ for the specific type checked and not the base classes.\r\n\r\nI suspect the `static_assert` will fail even in the existing build on Android and web, let me try.\r\n\r\nUPDATE:\r\nYes, I can confirm, the Android build even without this PR fails with:\r\n```\r\nstatic_assert(std::is_same<std::decay_t<T>, typename T::self_type>::value, \"T must use GDCLASS\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo some options:\r\n* Omit this `static_assert` (that's after all the current situation)\r\n* Put in a special case for `NO_SAFE_CAST`\r\n* Add a compile time warning that `cast_to()` will not work with the hierarchy for non-GDCLASS objects.\r\n\r\nI must admit it seems slightly hacky that the current behaviour seems different for non-GDCLASS objects depending on platform, and it would be nice to unify this, so I'd be tempted to go for emitting a warning when used for non-GDCLASS derived objects.\r\n\r\nAn alternative might be to see if these two cases can be modified to have them GDCLASS so the whole system works as is. That might be better, will have an investigate.\r\n\r\nLet me know any thoughts.","created_at":"2025-03-31T09:15:57Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T09:50:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020674339","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020674339"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020674339"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020674339/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":622,"original_line":622,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2020660695,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020730922","pull_request_review_id":2728768113,"id":2020730922,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc54cegq","diff_hunk":"@@ -609,30 +609,24 @@ class Object {\n \n \ttemplate <class T>\n \tstatic T *cast_to(Object *p_object) {\n-#ifndef NO_SAFE_CAST\n-\t\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\n-#else\n+\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_base_of<Object, T>::value, \"T must be derived from Object\");","path":"core/object.h","commit_id":"be6f971f4ff7b3647ac576ddc5813d462fe6fec9","original_commit_id":"429f1a82b012c3ebd40bab335c5a234cd72cf04b","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yes, it is possible to make it compile with the static assert by making 3 or 4 of these `Object` derived classes into `GDCLASS`.\r\n\r\nI guess you had the same problem on 4.x, but with the difference that you were able to revert to `dynamic_cast` in these cases, which it looks like we can't easily do on 3.x.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how much extra boiler plate `GD_CLASS` is adding and whether this is actually a problem in practice. The alternative would seem to be just to emit a warning during compilation on those platforms. :thinking: ","created_at":"2025-03-31T09:50:05Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T09:50:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020730922","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020730922"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020730922"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020730922/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":622,"original_line":622,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2020660695,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020737829","pull_request_review_id":2728780061,"id":2020737829,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc54cgMl","diff_hunk":"@@ -609,30 +609,24 @@ class Object {\n \n \ttemplate <class T>\n \tstatic T *cast_to(Object *p_object) {\n-#ifndef NO_SAFE_CAST\n-\t\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\n-#else\n+\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_base_of<Object, T>::value, \"T must be derived from Object\");","path":"core/object.h","commit_id":"be6f971f4ff7b3647ac576ddc5813d462fe6fec9","original_commit_id":"429f1a82b012c3ebd40bab335c5a234cd72cf04b","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It sounds like the bug already exists, and the `static_assert` is just uncovering it. \r\nIs there a reason `NO_SAFE_CAST` isn't supported on those platforms? Perhaps the right call is to remove it altogether and still fall back to `dynamic_cast` like in 4.x.\r\nFor 4.x I'm thinking I might introduce a \"soft\" `GDCLASS` which will just support casting by overriding the function, without all the other `GDCLASS` stuff. This would also solve these cases.","created_at":"2025-03-31T09:54:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T11:00:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020737829","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020737829"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020737829"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020737829/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":622,"original_line":622,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2020660695,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020808915","pull_request_review_id":2728893891,"id":2020808915,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc54cxjT","diff_hunk":"@@ -609,30 +609,24 @@ class Object {\n \n \ttemplate <class T>\n \tstatic T *cast_to(Object *p_object) {\n-#ifndef NO_SAFE_CAST\n-\t\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\n-#else\n+\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_base_of<Object, T>::value, \"T must be derived from Object\");","path":"core/object.h","commit_id":"be6f971f4ff7b3647ac576ddc5813d462fe6fec9","original_commit_id":"429f1a82b012c3ebd40bab335c5a234cd72cf04b","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Maybe there's no RTTI on them, I'm not sure - 3.x is compiled for a lot more low end devices than 4.x. I think in general avoiding `dynamic_cast` isn't a bad idea if we can do it.\r\n\r\nI do like the idea of a \"soft\" GDCLASS requirement might be a good balance.\r\n\r\nAnd in the unlikely case that there are a few modules that need this, it wouldn't be a great deal, and might fix some bugs, as you say, it's actually a pre-existing bug trap currently.","created_at":"2025-03-31T10:42:37Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T10:42:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020808915","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020808915"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2020808915"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2020808915/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":622,"original_line":622,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2020660695,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2021827946","pull_request_review_id":2730607944,"id":2021827946,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc54gqVq","diff_hunk":"@@ -609,30 +609,24 @@ class Object {\n \n \ttemplate <class T>\n \tstatic T *cast_to(Object *p_object) {\n-#ifndef NO_SAFE_CAST\n-\t\treturn dynamic_cast<T *>(p_object);\n-#else\n+\t\tstatic_assert(std::is_base_of<Object, T>::value, \"T must be derived from Object\");","path":"core/object.h","commit_id":"be6f971f4ff7b3647ac576ddc5813d462fe6fec9","original_commit_id":"429f1a82b012c3ebd40bab335c5a234cd72cf04b","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Maybe there's no RTTI on them, I'm not sure - 3.x is compiled for a lot more low end devices than 4.x. I think in general avoiding dynamic_cast isn't a bad idea if we can do it.\r\n\r\n```\r\n$ rg \"\\-f.*rtti\"\r\nplatform/javascript/detect.py\r\n96:        env.Append(CCFLAGS=[\"-fno-rtti\"])\r\n\r\nplatform/android/detect.py\r\n178:        env.Append(CXXFLAGS=[\"-frtti\"])\r\n180:        env.Append(CXXFLAGS=[\"-fno-rtti\"])\r\n```\r\n\r\nRTTI is disabled to keep the binary size low on web and android templates. Android editor uses RTTI as the editor itself needed it until this PR (presumably).","created_at":"2025-03-31T21:53:38Z","updated_at":"2025-03-31T21:53:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2021827946","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2021827946"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104825#discussion_r2021827946"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104825"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2021827946/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":622,"original_line":622,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2020660695,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":24,"subject_type":"line"}]